            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0358" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–1046: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-10">October 10,
                        1946</date>.<lb/>[Received October 10—2:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1628. Embassy spokesman made following announcement at 6:30 p.m., October 9:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“General Marshall flew to Shanghai this morning to see General Chou En Lai
                        and conferred with him there. General Marshall returned to Nanking at 6
                        p.m.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
